{
  "question_num": 1,
  "total_marks": 7,
  "title": "Kinematics",
  "main_stem": "A well has a depth of $36\\text{ m}$ from ground level to the surface of the water in the well, as shown in Fig. 1.1.\n\nFig. 1.1 (not to scale)\n\nA student wishes to find the depth of the well. The student plans to drop a stone down the well and record the time taken from releasing the stone to hearing the splash made by the stone as it enters the water.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Assume that air resistance is negligible and that the stone is released from rest.\n\nCalculate the time taken for the stone to fall from ground level to the surface of the water.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "The time recorded by the student using a stop-watch is not equal to the time in (a).\n\nSuggest **three** possible reasons, other than the effect of air resistance, for this difference.",
      "marks": 3,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "The student repeats the experiment three times and uses the results to calculate the depth of the well. The values are shown in Table 1.1.\n\nTable 1.1\n\n|  | 1st experiment | 2nd experiment | 3rd experiment |\n| depth/$\\text{m}$ | $54.4$ | $53.9$ | $54.1$ |\n\nThe true depth of the well is $36.0\\text{ m}$. Explain why these results may be described as precise but not accurate.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "use of $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^{2}$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$t = 2.7\\text{ s}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)",
      "marks": 3,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B3",
          "text": "Any three from: delay between hearing the splash and stopping the stop-watch; (splash) takes time to reach the student or the stone hits the water at a different time to the sound / sound (of the splash) has to travel to the student; not let go of the stone from ground level; not let go of the stone and start the stop-watch at the same time; stop-watch may not be properly calibrated / has a zero error; $g$ is not (exactly) $9.81\\text{ (m s}^{-2}\\text{)}$; stone given velocity / initial velocity not zero; stone does not fall (exactly) vertically / in a straight line"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "values are close together / have little scatter"
        },
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "values are not close to / $50\\%$ different / (very) different from the true value"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
